source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira renders the line below a heading item as a second block inside the item. JFM has no such item, so jiro keeps the heading in the item, writes the paragraph after the list, and warns about the containment it could not keep.
-- input.jira --
* h1. y
z
-- rendered.html --
<ul>
	<li><h1><a name="y"></a>y</h1>
<p>z</p></li>
</ul>
-- want.md --
- # y

z
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 2,
    "Column": 1,
    "Construct": "list",
    "Reason": "Jira keeps this line inside the list item above it; a JFM item holds nothing after its line control, so the line follows the list"
  }
]
